          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The average number of daylight hours per day in City 2 decreases from January, reaching a minimum of about 9 hours in June. It then increases, reaching a maximum of about 15 hours in December."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.15,
            0.847,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The maximum and minimum values in City 1 are more extreme than those of City 2. That is, the maximum number of daylight hours per day of City 1 is more than that of City 2, and the minimum number of daylight hours per day of City 1 is less than that of City 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.231,
            0.847,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In June, City 1 experiences daylight for about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " th of the full day (24 hours), whereas during December – January, it only experiences daylight for about "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " th of the full day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.298,
            0.76,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does this give some idea of where these two cities are located?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.325,
            0.848,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "City 1 and City 2 are located away from the Equator in the Northern and Southern hemispheres, respectively. City 1 is Helsinki, Finland, and City 2 is Wellington, New Zealand. These are also shown on the map. In June, the Northern Hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun, resulting in longer daylight hours; it is summertime here. Meanwhile, the Southern Hemisphere is tilted away from the Sun, leading to shorter days; it is winter time here. The inverted seasonal daylight pattern is due to the cities’ location in opposite hemispheres. The large variation in the data is because they are away from the Equator."
            }
          ]
        },
